{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-08-27",
  "note": "Which Civgraph election each Belfast newspaper Statement of Persons Nominated belongs to. Keyed by the OCR file stem in archive/ocr/. NOT used by the build or the site: this is review material for a publication decision that has not been taken.",
  "provenance": {
    "sourceMaterial": "Scans of Belfast newspapers held by the British Newspaper Archive. The BL_ file stems encode the BNA title id and the issue date; the issue date is the only date here that is not model-derived.",
    "extraction": "Raw OCR text was passed to an LLM by scripts/extract_spn_llm.py via OpenRouter, which wrote the structured JSON in archive/ocr/. THE EXTRACTION IS NOT RELIABLE: read against the scan, BL_0000038_19541123 carries one candidate and the extraction has two, the second wholly fabricated along with its proposer, seconder and agent address. An earlier trace test reported no fabrication; it was too permissive and its conclusion is retracted. Use data/database/spn-verified.json, transcribed by reading the scans, wherever a file appears in it.",
    "mappingMethod": "Proposed by scripts/review/match-spn-ocr-candidates.mjs, NOT by hand and NOT from the LLM's own election_name field, which is wrong on at least three records. Each OCR file was scored against every Civgraph contest within 120 days of the newspaper's issue date by the share of candidate surnames the two have in common. Only files scoring >= 0.75 are recorded as mappings; the rest are listed under `unresolved` rather than guessed.",
    "rightsPosition": "Established 2026-08-28 from the rights footers printed on the scans themselves (36 of 77 carry one), naming two holders: 'Image (c) National World Publishing Ltd' and 'Image (c) Independent News and Media PLC', both 'created courtesy of THE BRITISH LIBRARY BOARD', across 24 newspaper titles. THE IMAGES ARE THIRD-PARTY COPYRIGHT AND MUST NOT BE PUBLISHED; the source PDFs stay gitignored and no image is held here. The extracted FACTS are a separate question: a Statement of Persons Nominated is a statutory public notice published by a Returning Officer, the newspaper's typographical copyright is 25 years and so expired for all of these (latest 1988), and there is no copyright in facts. That is a considered position, not a clearance, and warrants one qualified review before publication -- but it is not what is blocking this. The data quality is.",
    "reOcr": "archive/ocr/text-v2/ holds a column-aware re-OCR (scripts/ocr/reocr-spn-columns.py, Tesseract --psm 4 plus a sparse --psm 11 supplement). It recovers 25.4% more Civgraph-known surnames than the original pass, improving 60 of 77 pages. The mappings below were computed from the ORIGINAL extraction and have not been recomputed: doing so requires re-running extract_spn_llm.py against text-v2, which needs an OpenRouter key.",
    "withdrawnNominations": "A Statement of Persons Nominated lists everyone nominated, INCLUDING those whose nominations were withdrawn and who never appeared on a ballot. 14 of the 77 scans carry withdrawn-nomination language, and they cluster in the low-scoring files. Civgraph's election data is derived from RESULTS and structurally cannot contain those people, so a withdrawn nominee correctly fails to join. A share of the 252 unmatched surnames are this, not extraction damage -- which means the match rate alone was never the right measure."
  },
